  "note": "Borough election, 21 January 1928, the first under Bangor's borough charter. Four members were returned for each ward from a single poll per ward; the new council then chose one member from each ward as alderman (Johnston-Kee, Davidson, Malcolm, Cathy and Gray). Four seats; W. Malcolm was afterwards chosen alderman for the ward. Only one vote separated J. Neill (378) from J. M. Thomson (377)."
